tebook explores when research inquiries necessitate abandonment or discontinuation, identifying technical integrity risks and failing rigorous validation as two primary criteria. It distinguishes between external environment changes (e.g., concept drift) and internal reasoning flaws (e.g., unreproducible result…", "title": "Criteria for Research Abandonment in Automated Inquiry"}, {"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01-v1", "project": "project-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-5913cf1feb0f47af", "source-a83824a2e359487c"], "revision": 1, "summary": "Examines how foundational assumptions in automated reasoning fail when evidentiary landscapes shift, relying on data source drift and communication network resilience.", "title": "Vulnerability of Foundational Assumptions in Automated Reasoning"}, {"id": "notebook-consensus-01-v1", "project": "project-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-5913cf1feb0f47af", "source-a83824a2e359487c", "source-bd255bafc0e046dc"], "revision": 3, "summary": "This revision synthesizes how autonomous agents should evaluate disagreement. It identifies that consensus among peers does not guarantee accuracy when underlying data sources are subject to drift, necessitating that agents prioritize independent empirical validation. Research into multi-robot and cyberphysical networ…", "title": "Rational Responses to Epistemic Peer Disagreement"}, {"id": "notebook-discovery-01-v1", "project": "project-discovery-01", "provenance": ["source-5913cf1feb0f47af", "source-ba72446ac5814f8a", "source-ac740e382ba34419"], "revision": 8, "summary": "Automated data science practices provide a structured mechanism for identifying research problems by synthesizing large-scale domain data. When applied to fields such as carbon-capturing technology, this approach successfully isolates alternative processes as novel research targets. This framework reduces reliance on …", "title": "Data-Driven Identification of Novel Research Domains"}, {"id": "notebook-reasoning-limits-01-v1", "project": "project-reasoning-limits-01", "provenance": ["source-5913cf1feb0f47af", "source-e4972e00c8e1484e"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Reasoning limits are implicitly defined by the operational boundaries of the collector and the stability of the input environment. Beyond architectural limitations, concept drift in data sources poses an unrecognized risk where agents reason on obsolete premises without internal signal of the shift.", "title": "Metacognitive Monitoring for Unrecognized Reasoning Limits"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "d6eec17f2b1d924f20c30e631eaef14e3dc8a575a9b32f129bf7c7ca28661a6a", "hash": "4e935c8860b78c4dfaebea2718b3163c4b43853a0332c71fa084200bd7019b58"}, {"seq": 3475, "time": "2026-10-29T19:02:32.153447+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 47136, "provider_input_hash": "821c0beb51ccac0c46e964b9a78768d26367a3c5015d6bd0d5dc2dcab8108c99", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-bf1fe35d482b4502"}, "prev_hash": "4e935c8860b78c4dfaebea2718b3163c4b43853a0332c71fa084200bd7019b58", "hash": "8fe33e3628a8d327fd141802b02029a9e536165c229b97065a09e981b61f2531"}, {"seq": 3476, "time": "2026-10-29T19:05:19.370145+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 47136, "provider_input_hash": "821c0beb51ccac0c46e964b9a78768d26367a3c5015d6bd0d5dc2dcab8108c99", "result": "rate_limited", "retry_after_seconds": 59.993115186691284}, "effect_accounting": 1, "id": "w-bf1fe35d482b4502"}, "prev_hash": "8fe33e3628a8d327fd141802b02029a9e536165c229b97065a09e981b61f2531", "hash": "c98331d6824abb478cc992c0d60bbf72a764b